+# lt03lte validation, 2026-10-26
+
+## WebView rendering
+
+Platform change: `system/core` commit `3cd368f`,
+`libcutils: recognize sealed memfds when sandbox blocks readlink`.
+
+On the tablet, WebView 155 failed to render because its sandbox denied
+`readlink(/proc/self/fd/N)` with EPERM. libcutils misclassified a sealed memfd
+as ashmem and aborted the renderer. The change permits the existing
+`F_GET_SEALS` check after EPERM/EACCES, retaining the mandatory grow/shrink
+seals. Other readlink errors still fail.
+
+The corrected library was temporarily bind-mounted on the running tablet.
+After restarting zygote, HTML and a JavaScript/Canvas animation rendered
+successfully, with the renderer process remaining alive.
+
+The full system image subsequently built successfully. Its libcutils matches
+the build staging file; disassembly confirms the permission-error fallback
+and required seal checks. The signed recovery package passed CRC and image
+hash checks. The rebuilt image has not been installed or boot-tested.
+
+## Acoustic analysis utility
+
+`tools/acoustic-check.py` analyzes an actual PCM16 WAV recording for the test
+sequence: 700 Hz, silence, 1100 Hz, silence, 1700 Hz, silence; one second per
+segment. It checks tone energy, separation from the following silence, and
+the proportion of signal power at each expected frequency.
+
+Checks performed:
+
+- Existing tablet recording: all samples zero; rejected.
+- Original generated stimulus: all three tones detected (analysis sanity check).
+- Synthetic delayed stimulus with noise: detected.
+- Synthetic continuous tones without the silence pattern: rejected.
+- Synthetic noise alone: rejected.
+
+These checks validate the analysis utility, not tablet speaker or microphone
+operation. A new physical microphone recording must still pass after the
+codec fixes are tested.
+
+## Changes excluded from the tested set
+
+The microphone/codec corrections only passed compilation. Speaker audibility,
+microphone input, sleep/resume stability, and VoLTE bidirectional call audio
+remain unverified. The tablet lost USB connectivity during a sleep/wake test;
+this does not establish whether the kernel hung or remained suspended.
+
+No unverified kernel changes are included with this validation commit.
